    "intro_html":  "Seco de pollo is the Sunday chicken stew of Ecuador, and the name is a little joke, since seco means dry and this is anything but. Achiote turns the whole pot a deep orange, citrus and a long slow braise break the chicken down until it falls off the fork, and a genuinely enormous amount of cilantro goes in at the end. Over rice, each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e590 calories and 56 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.65\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). That is a genuinely high protein number for a stew over rice.",
